cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TEAM, please cite it as below."
title: "TEAM: Transport Equity and Access Model"
version: 0.8.0
abstract: >-
  Travel times from every populated part of twenty New Zealand cities and
  towns, with the land that commutes into them, to everyday services and jobs by walking, low-stress cycling and public
  transport, at three times of day and under a fare budget; the people beyond
  stated access standards, how far short they are and how that falls by
  deprivation, income, age, car ownership, ethnicity and disability; fares
  against local income; and screening reasons that point to the kind of change
  that would bring each place within reach.
authors:
